{"title":"2025 WSMO Team Round Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> as the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/8/fb823b46da648a2378867a48c1279679b3acc50a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+ \\dots +f(2025).\\]\" width=\"276\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be positive reals such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/418ee06b264a855938f3de7cdd8c4a3474fcd856.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a}+\\frac{1}{b}=\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"38\" />. Find the minimum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many distinct ways are there to arrange the letters in SOLSTICE such that no two vowels are adjacent and the resulting word does not begin or end with a vowel.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For how many positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e865ce02c09e2e48661715824a17ab6a30e7b202.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\le2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" /> does <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/d/22d941691f1efb7755e6042c088dc92ddb2d5244.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^6$\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> divide evenly into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f156c838ae7d194e36ebf402316e89d42740431a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Anna picks two distinct prime numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f40a674e717c69679dcfba255e218168e9a12f5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&gt;q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/a/6aa32c77e0db28dbbc1c6612a5996cde5835adf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = pq(p-q) &lt; 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"20\" />. She tells Bob the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, but Bob is not able to uniquely determine the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Find the largest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/5/b05725a6508fe8df761c6e91d2735b697ebd87d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> be a function from the positive integers to the integers defined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/f/45fb0ec43d60198c4a6833f2e58b2d402a3e158b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d(n) = \\sum_{m&gt;0 \\text{ divides } n} (-1)^{d(m)}.\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"38\" /> Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50f92a6aa19649a285397e871df78cd5863d5552.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(30^{9})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c79701b36831dd0ffb63cd1498b0341b453a62b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_n\\}_{n\\ge 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/6/ba61693cc35f92673a8e22916187f42966c3f483.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{b_n\\}_{n\\ge 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" /> be sequences of real numbers with the property that for every positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef7576a651b488b33cbce006c7200deadeefc21.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{n+1}a_n = b_{n+1}b_n + b_{n+1}a_n + a_{n+1}b_n.\\]\" width=\"281\" height=\"17\" /> Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd8aea6a474725b9d95d292707e9ae63ea04aea2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/8/4d8f64764eaf5ef4f0381d00f2c5b30279de58ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/a/ada172fb83d62252931429d9ec3aa0a011c5ead2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{100} = 2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" />, find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/f/13f31325c315b40092f883dcf986cefb178c7a3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a trapezoid with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/0/1201da5496d8015043ddbcbd2ea89782fcc5a3b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB \\parallel CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" />. Circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> have diameters <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, and are tangent at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/b/18b8e4e7ae53228c09941f615336fef71f5e324c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA=3$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/a/aeaae437be614264fb9f8e08c66f50702583bbfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/926bbf02d6ee56f03f56fe748c7e128574f49201.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec36d3d67ce7715583346036c184d1b459adf874.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PD^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"17\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85ea1ad780a799bdaf8f327e664f65eb6f3546b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"18\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be a positive integer such that the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/d/fbdd04a120bf491fccac6f381976afda01b4dfa1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left \\lfloor \\frac{k}{\\left \\lfloor \\tfrac{k}{n} \\right \\rfloor} \\right \\rfloor = n\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"53\" /> has exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> positive integer solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Find the largest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be complex numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d938fc4d264b78693b353d9e47e2596bfdb5f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a|=|b|=|c|=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />. Suppose that the three summations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/0/2f04ab0e294ce7f0658ea7fbf97ea5223f44ddec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=0}^5 a^ib^{5-i}, \\ \\sum_{i=0}^7 b^ic^{7-i}, \\ \\text{and} \\  \\sum_{i=0}^{11} c^ia^{11-i}\\]\" width=\"288\" height=\"50\" /> are all nonzero real numbers. Find the number of possible ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be collinear in that order such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/4/bf4f26182ce276bf3f592d12dc9d55b85e97be46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 7$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/f/32ff6896ac10b4da9f3df84c2bccc3893cab6f5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />. Additionally, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be collinear in that order such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f5c097c7d31a2dfeda6611937a4d109e078ad7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BN = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91ad89046e9d6b2654aa563659330182c256f12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN = 3$\" width=\"69\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa1c8b561adfb6a2cc33d189227f3f70b2cf9777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NP \\perp AN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad8c355c7931b802254a4d6571e749c4e49709bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NP = MC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> vary, the set of all possible points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> traces out a convex region with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7b6b9d217194b2a79485901cdf525545aa5898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2025 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 11\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/b/5ebd0ac6384d8e0abac9179b0720864171445902.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_ n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> denote the sum of all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/4/d6444aeabe8cb1c6f4041690b1c121a3c7825192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{n}{m-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"35\" height=\"21\" /> is a positive integer. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive integer such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aedadf89acbfb68f9d146b61a10a1fc312bfb957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{2k} = 1650$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d8a34e5ebc76330808ef74c4c6be6193245fff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{4k} = 3492$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/7/037071847f112801d4ea99e8c44796144fca3bca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{8k} = 7158$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb3952afb04a37416e643cb0a6441935ee39d2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2025 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 12\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a rhombus. Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and is tangent to sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, respectively. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> distinct from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> are the intersections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> with sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31cd391bebc36897a8c10ea78e5d584980b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/6/bd652fd6084b903bf7381a774ad7750c1c895b96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/f/1ef58f566ea9a0a2aec446fc8c0993029bf2d8d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />, the square of the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85ea1ad780a799bdaf8f327e664f65eb6f3546b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"18\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2025 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 13\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the number of ways we can place a number in each cell of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f78a88b587445031518fc346fb96f6240e55a316.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32\\times 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> grid such that the following three conditions are met:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Every positive integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/a/f8a167665b988ee11f339380f6f697a30831ab29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32^2$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> appears in the grid;</li>\n<li>For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cells of the grid such that no two lie in the same row or column, the sum of the numbers in those cells is always the same;</li>\n<li>The numbers in each row increase from left to right, and the numbers in each column increase from bottom to top.</li></ul>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2025 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 14\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a cyclic quadrilateral. Lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/4143f6e3d205b4ef852de019c0e8ecb2c42d8871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BPC$\" width=\"55\" height=\"12\" /> intersects sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/1/94185900419e82fd8c9e03652017c53deeb065fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/a/1ca03d13f9aec9dfe69c8f6af2075bcefee35647.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae1462da8d66fb02591f24ab6c40eb6a4d4e0993.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY = \\tfrac{14}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"74\" height=\"23\" />, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85ea1ad780a799bdaf8f327e664f65eb6f3546b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"18\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2025 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 15\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018003750\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.050 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.058 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 629/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size